    <div class="seo-section prose">
      <section class="section" id="how">
        <h2>How the Daily Case Works</h2>
        <p>Every day GridPaw publishes one new murder sudoku case on this page. The puzzle is generated from the date itself, so there is no server queue, no lottery and no "first come" variant: everyone who opens the page on the same UTC day sees the same house, the same suspects and the same witness statements. Compare a deduction with a friend and you are looking at the same crime scene.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>One case a day, shared by everyone.</strong> The floor plan and statements come from a hash of the date, never from a random number. Two different browsers, two different countries, same board.</li>
          <li><strong>The case changes at 00:00 UTC.</strong> The countdown above the board is the exact time left on today's case. When it reaches zero, tomorrow's case opens automatically.</li>
          <li><strong>Weekdays are 4×4, weekends are 6×6.</strong> Monday to Friday runs a compact 4×4 house (three suspects); Saturday and Sunday unlock a 6×6 mansion with a fifth suspect and six rooms, which is a noticeably longer chain of deduction.</li>
          <li><strong>Every case has exactly one solution.</strong> Each daily puzzle is generated with a uniqueness proof and then checked against the witness statements before it is rendered, so guessing is never required — and never rewarded with an alternative answer.</li>
          <li><strong>The last seven days stay playable.</strong> The strip under the game keeps the current case plus the six before it. Earlier cases are retired: a backlog of old boards is not a daily puzzle.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Streaks: what counts and what does not</h3>
        <p>Your streak counts <strong>consecutive days on which you closed that day's case</strong>. Opening the page, reading the statements or replaying an old case does not extend it. Close today's case and the counter goes up by one; skip a full day and your next solve starts over at 1, while your best streak stays in the record. Everything is stored in your own browser, so there is no account, no email and no upload.</p>
        <h3>New to murder sudoku?</h3>
        <p>The daily case uses the same rules as the rest of the game: place every named suspect so that no two figures share a row or a column, follow the witness statements, and the suspect left alone with the victim is the killer. If you want the full rulebook with a solved example first, read <a href="/murder-sudoku/">how to play murder sudoku</a>, then warm up on <a href="/murdoku/">random practice cases</a> before coming back for tomorrow's daily.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="faq">
