        <details class="faq-item"><summary>What is the Murdoku daily case?</summary><div class="faq-answer">One murder sudoku case per day. The puzzle is generated from the date, so everyone who opens the page on the same UTC day gets the same floor plan and the same witness statements — you can compare notes with other detectives.</div></details>
        <details class="faq-item"><summary>When does the new daily case appear?</summary><div class="faq-answer">At 00:00 UTC every day. The countdown above the board shows the exact time left on today's case, and the last seven days stay playable in the archive strip.</div></details>
        <details class="faq-item"><summary>How does the daily streak work?</summary><div class="faq-answer">Your streak counts consecutive days on which you actually closed that day's case. Opening the page or playing a past case does not count. Miss a day and the streak resets to 1 on your next solve, while your best streak is kept.</div></details>
        <details class="faq-item"><summary>Is the daily case free and account-free?</summary><div class="faq-answer">Yes. The daily case is free, needs no account or download, and your streak is stored in your own browser with localStorage — nothing is uploaded.</div></details>
